HST Office: Table Properties with Word's tabs. Table, Row, Column, Cell and Alt Text come first; the settings
Word has elsewhere stay reachable behind them as Borders, Shading and Advanced (the old Text Flow page).

- Row applies height and "allow row to break" to the selected rows, the current one without a selection.
- Cell applies vertical alignment and margins to the selected cells and width to the current cell.
- Alt Text is the table format's grab bag (tblCaption, tblDescription). It round-trips through w:tblCaption and
  w:tblDescription in DOCX and through table:title and table:desc in ODF, and SetTableAttr makes it undoable.
- Page ids table, columns, borders, background, textflow are unchanged, and so are the moved widgets' ids.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); hsttable* are new files under MPL-2.0.
Test: tests/runtime/check-dialogs-writer.py table-properties table-rows table-wrap
